---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { tools, verticals, rankToolsForVertical, verticalFitScore, wrenchStackScore } from '../lib/data';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Disclosure', url: '/disclosure/' },
];

// Computed (2026-10-01). The page claimed "tools we earn $10,000 per signup on"
// (no program on the ledger pays that) and that unaffiliated tools "regularly" outrank
// them; both are replaced by counts from the data. "Active" uses the same test as the
// methodology ledger: a tracked http affiliate_url.
const isActive = (t: (typeof tools)[number]) => t.affiliate_url.startsWith('http');
const activeCount = tools.filter(isActive).length;
// A trade counts when none of the tools tied for first place on its trade page
// (same trade fit and same Fit Score as the first-ranked tool) has a tracked link.
const tradesTopUnaffiliated = verticals.filter((v) => {
  const ranked = rankToolsForVertical(v.slug);
  if (!ranked.length) return false;
  const top = ranked[0];
  const topGroup = ranked.filter(
    (t) =>
      verticalFitScore(t, v.slug) === verticalFitScore(top, v.slug) &&
      wrenchStackScore(t, v.slug) === wrenchStackScore(top, v.slug)
  );
  return !topGroup.some(isActive);
}).length;
---

<Layout
  title="Affiliate disclosure | WrenchStack"
  description="How WrenchStack makes money and the relationship between affiliate programs and rankings."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 prose prose-slate">
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>

    <p>
      WrenchStack may earn a commission when readers sign up with a vendor through a tracked link on our
      pages. Of the {tools.length} software tools in the directory, {activeCount} have a tracked affiliate
      link; the <a href="/methodology/#affiliate-ledger">per-vendor ledger</a> lists the status of every one.
      Reviews in the other categories state their affiliate status on the page. The vendor pays the
      commission; we add no charge of our own.
    </p>

    <h2>How affiliate relationships affect rankings</h2>

    <p>
      On each trade page, field-service software is ordered by fit for that trade, then by the
      <a href="/methodology/">WrenchStack Fit Score</a> (vertical fit 60%, pricing transparency 20%,
      integration coverage 20%), then by name. Neither the ordering nor the score has an input for
      affiliate status or commission rate. On {tradesTopUnaffiliated} of the {verticals.length} trade
      pages, none of the tools ranked first has a tracked affiliate link. Lead generation, insurance,
      payroll and marketing agencies are grouped by published tier rules that use verified facts only.
    </p>

    <h2>FTC disclosure</h2>

    <p>
      The FTC's
      <a href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/disclosures-101-social-media-influencers">Endorsement Guides</a>
      call for clear disclosure of material connections such as affiliate commissions. This page, the
      per-vendor ledger and the disclosure on each review are how we disclose ours.
      Affiliate links use <code>rel="sponsored"</code> in the page source. Outbound CTAs use
      <code>nofollow noopener</code> for security and search engine signaling.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>

    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:hello@wrenchstack.com">hello@wrenchstack.com</a> for corrections or
      clarifications. For vendor partnership inquiries, use <a href="mailto:partners@wrenchstack.com">partners@wrenchstack.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
